  "worked_solution": "The notation $a∣b$ means $a$ divides $b.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=ak.\n$$\n\n \nWith that in mind, let's examine our statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $x=-2$ and $y=1,$ we have $20(-2)+35(1)=-5,$ which is not divisible by $4.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that \n\n$$\n20x+35y=5(4x+7y).\n$$\n\nSince $x$ and $y$ are integers, $4x+7y$ must be an integer, too. So, $5$ divides $(20x+35y).$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $x=1$ and $y=0,$ we have $20(1)+35(0)=20,$ which is not divisible by $7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
